(function(){window.PhysicaRankPyqNeet_zoology_reproductivehealth=[{id:"neet-2026-q138",pn:138,y:"NEET 2026 \xB7 3 May",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"Assisted reproductive technologies",q:"Choose the correct statement regarding GIFT to overcome infertility.",o:["Ova collected from a female donor are transferred to the uterus of an infertile female.","It is the transfer of an ovum collected from a donor into the fallopian tube of another female who cannot produce ovum but can provide suitable environment for fertilization and development.","Early embryos with up to 8 blastomeres are transferred to the uterus of an infertile female.","Early embryos with up to 8 blastomeres are transferred into the fallopian tube of an infertile female."],c:1,s:`GIFT is an in-vivo technique used to assist infertility.
GIFT (Gamete Intra Fallopian Transfer) transfers an ovum collected from a donor into the fallopian tube of another female who cannot produce one but can provide a suitable environment for fertilization and further development.
ZIFT (Zygote Intra Fallopian Transfer) is an in-vitro technique in which the zygote or early embryo up to 8 blastomeres is transferred into the fallopian tube.`},{id:"neet-2026-q147",pn:147,y:"NEET 2026 \xB7 3 May",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"Contraceptive methods",q:`Match List I and List II
A. Progestasert \u2014 I. Barrier made of rubber used by females
B. Multiload 375 \u2014 II. Oral contraceptive
C. Diaphragm \u2014 III. Hormone releasing IUD
D. Saheli \u2014 IV. Copper releasing IUD`,o:["A(III), B(IV), C(I), D(II)","A(III), B(IV), C(II), D(I)","A(IV), B(II), C(I), D(III)","A(IV), B(III), C(I), D(II)"],c:0,s:`Progestasert is a hormone releasing IUD.
Multiload 375 is a copper releasing IUD.
Diaphragm is a barrier made of rubber used by females.
Saheli is an oral contraceptive.`},{id:"neet-2026r-q171",pn:171,y:"Re-NEET 2026 \xB7 21 Jun",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"Assisted reproductive technologies",q:"The method of directly of injecting a sperm into ovum in assisted reproductive technology is called:",o:["Zygote intra fallopian transfer (ZIFT)","Intra cytoplasmic sperm injection (ICSI)","Embryo transfer (ET)","Gamete intra fallopian transfer (GIFT)"],c:1,s:`ICSI is a procedure to form an embryo in the laboratory in which a sperm is injected directly into the ovum.
ZIFT transfers the zygote or early embryo (up to 8 blastomeres) into the fallopian tube.
GIFT transfers an ovum collected from a donor into the fallopian tube of another female who cannot produce one but can give a suitable environment for fertilisation and development.`},{id:"neet-2025-q093",pn:93,y:"NEET 2025",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"Assisted reproductive technologies, IVF",q:`What are the potential drawbacks in adoption of the IVF method?
A. High fatality risk to mother
B. Expensive instruments and reagents
C. Husband/wife necessary for being donors
D. Less adoption of orphans
E. Not available in India
F. Possibility that the early embryo does not survive
Choose the correct answer from the options given below:`,o:["B, D, F only","A, C, D, F only","A, B, C, D only","A, B, C, E, F only"],c:0,s:`Statements B, D and F are correct.
Statements A, C and E are incorrect.
Husband/wife is not necessary for being donors. IVF is available in India.`},{id:"neet-2024-q152",pn:152,y:"NEET 2024 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"Contraceptive methods (IUDs)",q:`Match List I with List II :
A. Non-medicated IUD \u2014 I. Multiload 375
B. Copper releasing IUD \u2014 II. Progestogens
C. Hormone releasing IND \u2014 III. Lippes loop
D. Implants \u2014 IV. LNG-20
Choose the correct answer from the options given below:`,o:["A-IV, B-I, C-II, D-III","A-III, B-I, C-IV, D-II","A-III, B-I, C-II, D-IV","A-I, B-III, C-IV, D-II"],c:1,s:`Lippes loop is a non-medicated IUD.
Multiload 375 is a copper releasing IUD.
LNG-20 is a hormone releasing IUD.
Progestogens are used as implants.
So A-III, B-I, C-IV, D-II.`},{id:"neet-2024-q175",pn:175,y:"NEET 2024 \xB7 5 May",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"Contraceptive methods",q:"Which of the following is not a natural/traditional contraceptive method?",o:["Lactational amenorrhea","Vaults","Coitus interruptus","Periodic abstinence"],c:1,s:`Option (2) is correct.
A vault is a rubber barrier method placed in the female tract to cover the cervix during coitus.
Lactational amenorrhea is natural: ovulation and cycles do not occur during intense lactation after childbirth.
Coitus interruptus is natural: the male withdraws before ejaculation.
Periodic abstinence is natural: couples avoid coitus in the fertile period.`},{id:"neet-2023-q152",pn:152,y:"NEET 2023 \xB7 7 May",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"RCH programme and amniocentesis",q:`Given below are two statement : one is labeled as Assertion A and the other is labeled as Reason R.
Assertion A : Amniocentesis for sex determination is one of the strategies of Reproductive and Child Health Care Programme.
Reason R : Ban on amniocentesis checks increasing menace of female foeticide.
In the light of the above statements, choose the correct answer from the options given below.`,o:["A is false but R is true.","Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A.","Both A and R are true and R is NOT the correct explanation of A.","A is true but R is false"],c:0,s:`The RCH programme spreads awareness about reproduction and gives facilities and support for a reproductively healthy society.
Amniocentesis is used to test for genetic disorders such as Down's syndrome and haemophilia, and to judge whether the foetus can survive.
It is not a sex determination method in India and not an RCH strategy, so A is false.
R is true: the ban on it checks female foeticide.`},{id:"neet-2023-q168",pn:168,y:"NEET 2023 \xB7 7 May",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"Sexually transmitted infections",q:"Which one of the following common sexually transmitted diseases is completely curable when detected early and treated properly ?",o:["HIV Infection","Genital herpes","Gonorrhoea","Hepatitis-B"],c:2,s:`Apart from hepatitis-B, genital herpes and HIV infection, other STIs are completely curable if found early and treated well.
Gonorrhoea is bacterial and can be cured.
The other three are viral.`},{id:"neet-2023-q185",pn:185,y:"NEET 2023 \xB7 7 May",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"Contraceptive methods",q:`Match List I with List II.
List I: A. Vasectomy; B. Coitus interruptus; C. Cervical caps; D. Saheli
List II: I. Oral method; II. Barrier method; III. Surgical method; IV. Natural method
Choose the correct answer from the options given below:`,o:["A-IV, B-II, C-I, D-III","A-III, B-I, C-IV, D-II","A-III, B-IV, C-II, D-I","A-II, B-III, C-I, D-IV"],c:2,s:`Vasectomy is a surgical method.
Coitus interruptus is a natural method.
Cervical cap is a barrier method.
Saheli is an oral, non-steroidal pill.`},{id:"neet-2022-q172",pn:172,y:"NEET 2022 \xB7 17 Jul",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"Intrauterine devices",q:"Lippe's loop is a type of contraceptive used as:",o:["Vault barrier","Non-Medicated IUD","Copper releasing IUD","Cervical barrier"],c:1,s:`Lippes loop is a non-medicated IUD.
Copper-releasing IUDs are CuT, Cu7 and multiload 375.
Diaphragms, cervical caps and vaults are barrier methods.`},{id:"neet-2022-q200",pn:200,y:"NEET 2022 \xB7 17 Jul",tp:"Reproductive Health",st:"Contraception methods",q:"Match List \u2013 I with List \u2013 II with respect to methods of contraception and their respective actions. (a) Diaphragms (b) Contraceptive Pills (c) Intra Uterine Devices (d) Lactational Amenorrhea ; (i) Inhibit ovulation and implantation (ii) Increase phagocytosis of sperm within Uterus (iii) Absence of Menstural cycle and ovulation following parturition (iv) They cove the cervix blocking the entry of sperms",o:["(a) - (iv), (b) - (i), (c) - (ii), (d) - (iii)","(a) - (ii), (b) - (iv), (c) - (i), (d) - (iii)","(a) - (iii), (b) - (ii), (c) - (i), (d) - (iv)","(a) - (iv), (b) - (i), (c) - (iii), (d) - (ii)"],c:0,s:`Diaphragms are barriers that cover the cervix and block sperm entry.
Pills (progestogen or progestogen with oestrogen) inhibit ovulation and implantation and thicken cervical mucus.
IUDs increase phagocytosis of sperm in the uterus.
Lactational amenorrhoea: no ovulation or periods during intense lactation after childbirth.
So a-iv, b-i, c-ii, d-iii.`}]})();
